
*-key.json
*.log

# Local data — never publish
morning_bets.db
# Derived from the play-by-play cache; rebuilds in ~30s. Never the
# authority on anything, which is why it is a separate file.
context.db
context.db-wal
context.db-shm
# WAL mode puts the hot pages in a sibling file; the exact-name rule above
# does not cover them.
morning_bets.db-wal
morning_bets.db-shm
bets/*.json
# EXCEPT the printed boards. A `_board.json` is the frozen record of what we
# said AND what Kalshi's mid was at print time, and the mid is unrecoverable
# once the market moves — it is the evidence TODO item 14's falsifier is
# scored against. ~85 KB a night.
!bets/*_board.json
# The rendered page is ~175 KB a night and rebuilds from that JSON in one
# second, so it is a render and not a record. Same argument as
# `scratchpad/board_*.html` below.
bets/*_board.html
bets/*_graded.md
sent.json
.cron-config

